    "explanation": "Trip TRP-00102 (Woodlands to ION Orchard, 19 July 2026) is a route-deviation dispute, and I decide it on the fare rules rather than on which route either of you would have chosen.\n\nFor the rider: under POL-RD-01 a route deviation is refundable only when the excess distance over the booked optimal route is BOTH more than 20% of that optimal route AND more than 0.8 km; both limbs must pass. On the governing figure — the GPS trace distance of 21.79 km measured against the 20.4 km optimal (the trip record's 21.8 km is a rounded convenience copy and may not be used for the test) — the excess is 1.39 km, or 6.81%. That clears the 0.8 km limb but fails the 20% limb, so no route deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 says the outcome is NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. Your complaint is really about elapsed time (32 minutes against a 27-minute estimate) and about the route you would have taken; the refund rule is a distance rule, so neither supports a refund.\n\nYou also say the driver's explanation — a BKE crawl — has nothing behind it. On the record that is correct: EV-ADVIS-00102-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, severity BLOCKING) is absent, and its own issue detail confirms no LTA advisory covers the BKE or the Upper Bukit Timah corridor in the 11:16–11:55 window, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run. It changes nothing, because with no deviation established there was nothing for the driver to excuse. The driver's traffic explanation is a bare assertion that carries no evidence ID and is discarded under POL-RD-08; it is not a limb left untested. POL-RD-10 therefore does not fire: the trace is complete (193 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, none of the POL-RD-07(a)–(c) impairments), the trip identifiers and pickup/dropoff timestamps agree across the trip record, trace and ledger, and the missing advisory is not needed to decide this case. There is no ground to hold the disputed amount instead of ruling.\n\nFor the driver: your route was not a refundable deviation, so the SGD 29.91 fare stands and nothing is refunded to the rider. Your 11:29 message about Upper Bukit Timah was delivered and read, but the rider never instructed a route or gave a waypoint (waypoint_hint is null), so POL-RD-04 does not apply and no driver compensation is due — the distance billed (21.8 km) is not less than the trace records (21.79 km), so there is no unbilled shortfall to pay. There are no ERP gantries and no airport surcharge on this trip, so POL-RD-09 gives nothing to refund or correct.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. The fare stands as charged; fare_breakdown.payment_status (CHARGED) and refund_issued_sgd (0.0) are left exactly as they are."
  },
